  "notes": "West's spade lead is taken by East with the ♠A. East returns a spade, won in the dummy. South's only possible remaining loser is in the trump suit. South must avoid losing a trick to the ♥Q.\n\nA famous bridge saying can be used to remember the right play with this suit combination. 8 ever, 9 never tells us that when holding an 8 card fit including all of the top honours except the Queen, you should finesse against that card.\n\nWhen holding a 9 card fit missing just the Queen (as in this heart suit) it is correct to cash the top honours hoping the Queen is either singleton or doubleton.\n\nThe ♥A and ♥K should be cashed. When the ♥Q drops, South is rewarded for taking the correct percentage play. South can easily take the rest of the tricks.",
